WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.480
In your lungs, oxygen
loads onto your blood.

2
00:00:03.480 --> 00:00:07.900
In your tissues, where oxygen
is low, the blood lets it go.

3
00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:13.440
Now add a trace of carbon monoxide:
just 0.1 per cent of the air.

4
00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:16.000
There is still plenty
of oxygen to breathe.

5
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:18.580
Yet the tissues are starved of it.

6
00:00:18.580 --> 00:00:24.600
So how can a trace of one gas stop blood
carrying oxygen, with oxygen all around?

7
00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:27.860
In this mission, you'll swap
the ligands around a metal ion,

8
00:00:27.860 --> 00:00:31.940
and watch each solution change
shade as they trade places.

9
00:00:31.940 --> 00:00:38.460
Then you'll see why a ligand that holds on with several
bonds can push out ligands that hold on with only one.

10
00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:43.390
Your mission: explain how carbon
monoxide stops blood carrying oxygen.